		<item>
			<title>First Official Pic from Madonna Turn Up The Radio video being shoot in Mugello</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/782-first-official-pic-from-madonna-turn-up-the-radio-video-being-shoot-in-mugello.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/782-first-official-pic-from-madonna-turn-up-the-radio-video-being-shoot-in-mugello.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedImage"><img src="http://drownedmadonna.com//media/k2/items/cache/55d4420dd6cd56f2e756dd2f75804f62_S.jpg" alt="First Official Pic from Madonna Turn Up The Radio video being shoot in Mugello" /></div><div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>The shooting of <strong>Madonna Turn Up The Radio</strong> video started today. Here is the first official pic from the shooting in <strong>Mugello</strong>, Tuscany, Italy.</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Video clips</category>
			<pubDate>Mon, 18 Jun 2012 17:38:44 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Madonna Turn Up The Radio video shooting today and tomorrow in Florence</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/781-madonna-turn-up-the-radio-video-shooting-today-and-tomorrow-in-florence.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/781-madonna-turn-up-the-radio-video-shooting-today-and-tomorrow-in-florence.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p><strong>Madonna</strong> is shooting her <strong>Turn Up The Radio</strong> video in <strong>Florence</strong> today and tomorrow. Latest news are that <strong>Tom Munro</strong> is directing as we <a href="http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/776-exclusive-tom-munro-to-direct-madonnas-turn-up-the-radio-video.html">exclusively revealed</a> two weeks ago, but Jonas Akerlund is involved, including his wife.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>According to Italian press, Turn Up The Radio will be filmed in the historical centre of Florence and on the Arno river sides. The most impressive locations are mentioned as part of the shooting.</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Video clips</category>
			<pubDate>Mon, 18 Jun 2012 07:45:49 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Update: Jonas Akerlund is now directing Madonna Turn Up The Radio video. And Tom Munro?</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/779-update-jonas-akerlund-is-now-directing-madonna-turn-up-the-radio-video-and-tom-munro?.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/779-update-jonas-akerlund-is-now-directing-madonna-turn-up-the-radio-video-and-tom-munro?.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>EXCLUSIVE - When <a href="http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/776-exclusive-tom-munro-to-direct-madonnas-turn-up-the-radio-video.html">we revealed that Tom Munro</a> was the director of <strong>Madonna's Turn Up The Radio video</strong>, we omitted to report that <strong>Jonas Akerlund</strong> was the director at first.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Now we have learned that <strong>Jonas Akerlund</strong> is directed the music video for <strong>Turn Up The Radio</strong>, which is still planned for this weekend in Florence, if it is not going to be postponed again.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Anyway, keep in mind that we cannot exclude that there will be a last minute change again and <strong>Tom Munro</strong> is back on the project.</p>
<p> </p>
<p><strong>Akerlund</strong> directed <strong>Madonna</strong>'s videos for Ray of Light, Music, American Life and Jump. He also directed I'm Going to Tell You a Secret documentary and her Confessions Tour DVD.</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Video clips</category>
			<pubDate>Sat, 16 Jun 2012 10:15:35 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Madonna Turn Up The Radio video to be filmed this weekend in Florence</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/778-madonna-turn-up-the-radio-video-to-be-filmed-this-weekend-in-florence.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/778-madonna-turn-up-the-radio-video-to-be-filmed-this-weekend-in-florence.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>After being postponed, the video for <strong>Madonna's Turn Up The Radio</strong> will be filmed this weekend, as also MadonnaTribe.com confirms today and Madonna herself told Italian newspaper La Repubblica. This means the video-clip will be shoot in the impressive <strong>Florence</strong>, Italy.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>As DrownedMadonna.com already revealed, <strong>Turn Up The Radio</strong> will be directed by photographer <strong>Tom Munro</strong>.</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Video clips</category>
			<pubDate>Tue, 12 Jun 2012 07:18:25 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Madonna Turn Up The Radio video shooting directed by Tom Munro is postponed</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/777-madonna-turn-up-the-radio-video-shooting-directed-by-tom-munro-is-postponed.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/777-madonna-turn-up-the-radio-video-shooting-directed-by-tom-munro-is-postponed.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>They are still not ready for the shooting of <strong>Turn Up The Radio</strong>, therefore it is not taking place today as previously planned, reported and also confirmed by Live Nation Italia. They are still looking for a product placement deal, especially an automotive deal,  like Madonna did with Smirnoff in Give Me All Your Luvin' video and Jennifer Lopez had with FIAT in her  Papi video.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Maybe, the video shooting - directed by <strong>Tom Munro</strong> as we told you a few days ago - will happen next weekend.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Reports by Italian press regarding archeological areas in <strong>Rome</strong> were not true, in fact a car theme was part of the concept.</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Video clips</category>
			<pubDate>Sun, 10 Jun 2012 13:25:29 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>EXCLUSIVE: Tom Munro to direct Madonna Turn Up The Radio Video</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/776-exclusive-tom-munro-to-direct-madonnas-turn-up-the-radio-video.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/776-exclusive-tom-munro-to-direct-madonnas-turn-up-the-radio-video.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>EXCLUSIVE - DrownedMadonna.com heard more exclusive news on the <strong>music video</strong> of <strong>Madonna</strong>'s third single from MDNA, <strong>Turn Up The Radio</strong>.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>We learned that <strong>Madonna's Turn Up The Radio</strong> will be directed by famous photographer <strong>Tom Munro</strong>. <strong>Madonna</strong> already worked with <strong>Munro</strong> for several magazine shoots and her Give It 2 Me video.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>We remind you that the video will be filmed in Rome on Sunday, June 10, two days before her first Italian concert at the Olympic Stadium in Rome. <a href="http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/773-update-turn-up-the-radio-to-be-shoot-in-rome-and.html">Read what we previously reported</a>.</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Video clips</category>
			<pubDate>Thu, 07 Jun 2012 22:43:17 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Confirmed: Madonna to shoot the Turn Up the Radio video in Rome on June 10</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/775-confirmed-madonna-to-shoot-the-turn-up-the-radio-video-in-rome-on-june-10.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/775-confirmed-madonna-to-shoot-the-turn-up-the-radio-video-in-rome-on-june-10.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>BREAKING NEWS - Italian press is talking about the exclusive news (<a href="http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/759-madonnas-turn-up-the-radio-video-to-be-shoot-on-june-10.html">#1</a> and <a href="http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/773-update-turn-up-the-radio-to-be-shoot-in-rome-and.html">#2</a>) that DrownedMadonna.com published about the <strong>video</strong> shooting of <strong>Madonna's Turn Up The Radio</strong> in <strong>Rome</strong> on Sunday, June 10.</p>
<p>Today Live Nation Italia confirmed our news and also details on a product placement deal.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>"We are planning a video set in the archeological <strong>Rome</strong>," <strong>Madonna</strong>'s entourage confirmed today to Italian paper La Repubblica.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>"<strong>Madonna</strong>'s plans to shoot her video in <strong>Rome</strong> two days before her concert at the Olympic Stadium are true," Live Nation Italia Chief, Roberto De Luca, confirms this way our scoop. <strong>Turn Up The Radio video</strong> is planned to be set on Rome beautiful historical locations.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Roberto De Luca also confirms our news about a product placement deal that <strong>Madonna</strong> is trying to get, as she did with Smirnoff in Give Me All Your Luvin' video.</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Video clips</category>
			<pubDate>Wed, 06 Jun 2012 08:50:06 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
	</channel>
